{"agent_id":"agy-data-steward","role_summary":"Own longevity: versioning, provenance, reproducibility, migration, and the relationship between telemetry and the knowledge base so that evidence revisions and crop additions never destroy the ability to explain what a past dashboard displayed and why.","recommendation":"Separate telemetry and knowledge into two SQLite files sharing a common deployment_id foreign key. Version the knowledge base with an immutable append-only evidence_revision table keyed by (revision_id, fact_id) so every dashboard render can be replayed against the revision that was active at that timestamp. Keep the markdown documents as the canonical source of truth and treat the database as a derived, reproducible cache rebuilt by a deterministic extraction pipeline whose version is itself recorded in each revision.","why":["Telemetry is high-write append-only data (potentially millions of rows); knowledge is low-write read-heavy (~200 facts across 8 crops). Co-locating them in one SQLite file causes write contention and makes backup/retention policies incompatible.","Without an immutable revision table, any update to a crop's evidence silently changes what the dashboard would have shown last month, violating auditability (criterion 3).","Treating markdown as source of truth and the DB as a derived cache means document revisions (adding crops, correcting values) follow normal git review, and the extraction pipeline can be re-run to produce any historical snapshot.","The gap registry's evidence_status vocabulary is already a controlled enum; storing it per-fact-per-revision makes the recommended_ai_usage filtering rules executable as SQL JOINs rather than prose."],"schema_sketch":"-- FILE: knowledge.sqlite\n\nCREATE TABLE revision (\n  revision_id   INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  created_at    TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now')),\n  source_commit TEXT,          -- git SHA of backend/docs/cropinfo/\n  pipeline_ver  TEXT NOT NULL,  -- semver of extraction script\n  author        TEXT,\n  note          TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE crop (\n  crop_id       TEXT PRIMARY KEY,  -- e.g. 'basil'\n  scientific_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  display_name_ko TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE fact (\n  fact_id       INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  section       TEXT NOT NULL,       -- e.g. '2_atmospheric'\n  axis          TEXT NOT NULL,       -- e.g. 'air_temp_optimum'\n  value_type    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (value_type IN (\n    'optimum_range','single_point','injury_threshold',\n    'disease_risk','experimental_condition','absence'\n  )),\n  value_json    TEXT,                -- JSON: {\"min\":25,\"max\":30,\"unit\":\"C\"} or null for absence\n  unit          TEXT,\n  measurement_basis TEXT,            -- e.g. 'irrigation_water_EC', 'field_capacity_pct', 'pot_sensor_VWC'\n  growth_stage  TEXT,\n  cultivar      TEXT,\n  cultivation_system TEXT,           -- 'open_field','greenhouse_NFT','growth_chamber' etc.\n  source_ids    TEXT NOT NULL,       -- JSON array of source_record.source_id refs\n  original_text TEXT,                -- verbatim Korean excerpt for audit\n  UNIQUE(crop_id, section, axis, value_type, growth_stage, cultivar, cultivation_system)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE fact_evidence_status (\n  fact_id       INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES fact(fact_id),\n  status        TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (status IN (\n    'no_direct_evidence','cultivar_specific','system_specific',\n    'stage_specific','general_crop_reference',\n    'experimental_condition_only','measurement_not_transferable',\n    'not_a_risk_threshold','insufficient_duration_data',\n    'no_recovery_threshold'\n  )),\n  PRIMARY KEY (fact_id, status)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE fact_revision (\n  revision_id   INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES revision(revision_id),\n  fact_id       INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES fact(fact_id),\n  action        TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (action IN ('insert','update','delete')),\n  prev_value_json TEXT,  -- null on insert\n  new_value_json  TEXT,  -- null on delete\n  PRIMARY KEY (revision_id, fact_id)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE source_record (\n  source_id     INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  title         TEXT NOT NULL,\n  authors       TEXT,\n  year          INTEGER,\n  url           TEXT,\n  measurement_method TEXT,\n  applicable_env TEXT,   -- 'open_field','greenhouse','indoor'\n  cultivar_info TEXT,\n  limitations   TEXT\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE user_action (\n  action_id     INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  trigger_axis  TEXT,           -- which axis triggers this guidance\n  condition     TEXT,           -- e.g. 'soil_moisture_low'\n  guidance_ko   TEXT NOT NULL,  -- Korean prose from section 9\n  guidance_en   TEXT\n);\n\n-- VIEW: active facts at a given revision\nCREATE VIEW current_facts AS\nSELECT f.* FROM fact f\nWHERE NOT EXISTS (\n  SELECT 1 FROM fact_revision fr\n  WHERE fr.fact_id = f.fact_id AND fr.action = 'delete'\n    AND fr.revision_id = (SELECT MAX(revision_id) FROM revision)\n);\n\n-- FILE: telemetry.sqlite (separate file)\n\nCREATE TABLE deployment (\n  deployment_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id       TEXT NOT NULL,      -- FK enforced at app level\n  location      TEXT,\n  cultivation_system TEXT,\n  cultivar      TEXT,\n  created_at    TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE sensor_reading (\n  reading_id    INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  deployment_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES deployment(deployment_id),\n  channel       TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (channel IN (\n    'air_temperature','air_humidity','illuminance_lux',\n    'co2','particulate_matter','noise',\n    'soil_moisture','soil_temperature'\n  )),\n  value         REAL NOT NULL,\n  unit          TEXT NOT NULL,\n  recorded_at   TEXT NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE INDEX idx_reading_deploy_time ON sensor_reading(deployment_id, recorded_at);\n\nCREATE TABLE dashboard_snapshot (\n  snapshot_id     INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  deployment_id   TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES deployment(deployment_id),\n  revision_id     INTEGER NOT NULL,  -- which knowledge revision was used\n  rendered_at     TEXT NOT NULL,\n  score_payload   TEXT               -- JSON blob of computed scores for replay\n);\n\n-- Calibration lives here, clearly separated from literature\nCREATE TABLE sensor_calibration (\n  calibration_id  INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  deployment_id   TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES deployment(deployment_id),\n  channel         TEXT NOT NULL,\n  from_unit       TEXT NOT NULL,      -- e.g. 'lux'\n  to_unit         TEXT NOT NULL,      -- e.g. 'umol_m2_s'\n  method          TEXT NOT NULL,      -- e.g. 'linear_coefficient'\n  parameters_json TEXT NOT NULL,      -- e.g. {\"factor\": 0.0185, \"note\": \"white LED assumed\"}\n  valid_from      TEXT NOT NULL,\n  valid_until     TEXT,\n  created_by      TEXT NOT NULL\n);","scorable_axes":["air_temperature — basil has literature-cited optimum 25-30°C and injury threshold <12°C; lettuce has 18-24°C and quality risk >26.7°C","soil_temperature — stage-specific germination ranges exist for most crops, sufficient for germination-phase scoring only"],"unscorable_axes":["air_humidity — documented RH values are disease-risk thresholds (85%, 95%), not growth optima; scoring against them is a category error","illuminance_lux — all evidence is PPFD/DLI; lux-to-PPFD conversion is spectrum-dependent and unbacked","soil_moisture — field-capacity ratios and system-specific VWC are measurement_not_transferable to a generic capacitive sensor","co2 — only one basil CO2 interaction study across all 8 docs; no per-crop optima","particulate_matter — zero horticultural evidence in the corpus","noise — not a recognised crop growth factor; scoring it is pseudoscience"],"assumptions":["The extraction pipeline can be made deterministic enough that re-running it on the same markdown commit produces identical rows — this requires the Korean prose tables to be structurally regular, which the 254-line crops' identical skeleton suggests but must be verified.","Dashboard render frequency is low enough that recording a snapshot per render in dashboard_snapshot is feasible (dozens per day, not thousands).","The team can afford the overhead of two SQLite files instead of one; ATTACH DATABASE in SQLite makes cross-file JOINs possible if needed.","Git is available for source_commit provenance; if the team uses a different VCS or none, revision tracking degrades."],"risks":["Revision tracking adds schema complexity that may not be queried during the hackathon, incurring build cost for no immediate payoff.","Two-file separation requires the application layer to manage two connections or use ATTACH, which is slightly more complex than a single file.","If the extraction pipeline is not truly deterministic (e.g. LLM-assisted extraction introduces non-reproducibility), the revision chain becomes unreliable and the whole provenance model is undermined.","fact_revision only captures value changes, not schema migrations; if the fact table shape itself evolves, replay becomes harder."],"cheap_validation":"Pick one crop (lettuce, 254 lines). Manually extract all facts from the markdown into a spreadsheet with columns matching the fact table. Verify: (1) every row maps to exactly one value_type and at least one evidence_status, (2) no value is recorded without a source_id, (3) round-trip the spreadsheet back to markdown to confirm nothing is lost. Should take ~40 minutes.","change_mind_if":"If the team demonstrates they will never need to explain a past dashboard state — e.g. this is a demo-only prototype with no users retaining it — then the revision and snapshot tables are pure overhead and a single mutable knowledge.json file with telemetry in one SQLite is simpler and sufficient."}
